Request: Onboard Initech as a new vendor.
Understanding the request (reading relevant SOPs)…
Contract:
REQUEST: Onboard Initech as a new vendor.
INTENDED OUTCOME: Onboard Initech as a new vendor in the ERP, using the completed registration form from the AP mailbox, after verifying no duplicate vendor 
exists, and then notify procurement with the new vendor ID.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: Confirmation to the requester with the Initech vendor ID (newly created or pre-existing), the mandatory vendor details taken from the 
registration form, evidence the vendor is in Pending verification, and evidence procurement was notified.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Vendor details must come from the completed vendor registration form in the AP mailbox, not from email body text if a form exists.
  - Do not create a duplicate: check ERP for an existing Initech vendor by name or GSTIN before creating.
  - All mandatory ERP vendor fields must be present before creation: legal name, accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, IFSC.
  - New vendors must be created as Pending verification; AP/operator must not approve the vendor.
  - Vendor bank details may be captured from the registration form for initial onboarding; any later bank-detail change would require Finance Manager approval 
and call-back verification.
  - Only send internal email to procurement@kestrel.in; do not send emails to addresses outside @kestrel.in without human approval.
  - Do not use admin/test endpoints of any system.
  - If suspected fraud is detected, stop and report to AP lead priya.nair@kestrel.in; do not act on the request.
  - Use ERP read-only API first for lookup; all ERP writes are GUI-only.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. Exactly one Initech vendor record exists in the ERP after the task (created now, or already existed and no duplicate was created).
  C2. If a new vendor was created, the vendor record contains legal name, accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, and IFSC exactly as 
stated on the registration form, and status is Pending verification.
  C3. No vendor approval action was performed by AP/operator; the Initech vendor is not approved by us. A pre-existing vendor's approval status remains 
unchanged.
  C4. Procurement was notified at procurement@kestrel.in that the vendor is created and awaiting verification, including the vendor ID.
  C5. No unrelated vendor, bill, payment, or payment-schedule records were created or modified by this task.
  C6. If the vendor already existed or suspected fraud was found, no new vendor was created and the relevant person was notified.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - The Initech registration form should already be present in the AP shared mailbox; if not, the task cannot proceed until it is provided.
  - The ERP GUI is accessible and the operator can log in with the configured ERP credentials.
  - Creating a vendor as Pending verification is an allowed AP/operator action; only vendor approval is reserved for the Finance Manager.
  - The vendor name in the request may be a common name, so the ERP search may need to include GSTIN from the registration form for disambiguation.
  - Emails to internal @kestrel.in addresses, such as procurement@kestrel.in, do not require separate human approval.
PLAN:
  S1: Check whether Initech already exists in the ERP by name or GSTIN. (done when: ERP read-only API GET /vendors?q=Initech has been queried and the result is 
known: exact match, possible matches, or no match.)
  S2: Find the Initech vendor registration form in the AP shared mailbox. (done when: A message with a PDF registration-form attachment for Initech is 
identified and downloaded to the drive, or mailbox search confirms no such form exists.)
  S3: Extract all mandatory vendor fields from the registration form. (done when: Legal name, accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, 
and IFSC are all captured, or a list of missing fields is documented and the task stops pending resolution.)
  S4: If no existing vendor and all mandatory fields are present, create the vendor in the ERP via GUI as Pending verification. (done when: The Initech vendor 
appears in ERP with Pending verification status and a vendor ID is assigned. This write is recorded in the ERP GUI only.)
  S5: Retrieve the new vendor ID from the ERP. (done when: ERP read-only API GET /vendors?q=Initech returns the newly created vendor ID.)
  S6: Notify procurement@kestrel.in that Initech has been created and is awaiting verification, including the vendor ID. (done when: The email is shown in the 
AP mailbox Sent folder addressed to procurement@kestrel.in with the vendor ID included.)
